[
    {
        "content": "<p>The following code shows that there is an internal error or sorry when using variables that mention private definitions.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">module</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">linter</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">unusedSectionVars</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">false</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">expose</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">section</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">private</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hfoo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- error: internal exception #3 -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"n\">include</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hfoo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">private</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bar1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- error: internal exception #3 -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"n\">include</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hfoo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">private</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bar2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hfoo</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">//</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">})</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- warning: declaration uses `sorry` -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">private</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bar3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hfoo</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">//</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">})</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- info: \"4.30.0-rc2\" -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">versionString</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 592123439,
        "sender_full_name": "Floris van Doorn",
        "timestamp": 1777571692
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>( cc <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"110024\">@Sebastian Ullrich</span> - I hope it's ok to ping you)<br>\nLet me know if you'd like me to open an issue.</p>",
        "id": 592123711,
        "sender_full_name": "Floris van Doorn",
        "timestamp": 1777571768
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Note: removing <code>private</code> from <code>bar1</code> still gives an internal exception. The other two give nice error messages.</p>",
        "id": 592124120,
        "sender_full_name": "Floris van Doorn",
        "timestamp": 1777571909
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>might be related to <a class=\"message-link\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/113489-new-members/topic/Strange.20module.20system.20sorries/near/569150332\">#new members &gt; Strange module system sorries @ 💬</a></p>",
        "id": 592124789,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1777572070
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>If anyone wants to sanity-check my proposed solution in that thread, that would be helpful</p>",
        "id": 592308915,
        "sender_full_name": "Sebastian Ullrich",
        "timestamp": 1777650592
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Having separate <code>private variable</code> and <code>public variable</code> commands seems reasonable to me, and I think that would solve this issue.</p>\n<p>Another potential option is that each variable is automatically tagged to be <code>private</code> or <code>public</code> (depending on whether it uses something private), and that a user doesn't have to specify it manually.</p>",
        "id": 592466943,
        "sender_full_name": "Floris van Doorn",
        "timestamp": 1777743166
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>That's unfortunately not really tractable as the last example in the other thread shows: mere elaboration of the variable type can have side effects such as creating aux theorems for which we need to know the scope of the variable a priori</p>",
        "id": 592472003,
        "sender_full_name": "Sebastian Ullrich",
        "timestamp": 1777746129
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Well, we could try elaborating it in the public scope and try again in the private scope if that fails, but we're already elaborating variables more often than would be ideal!</p>",
        "id": 592472111,
        "sender_full_name": "Sebastian Ullrich",
        "timestamp": 1777746201
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It makes sense to me on a principle level, but what would the error message be to inform the user facing the following confusion:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">…</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- huh, where are my variables?</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 592488119,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Murrills",
        "timestamp": 1777758708
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>If we make sure that public auto implicits cannot shadow even private variables, we should be able to get the same explaining message as for declarations</p>",
        "id": 592546104,
        "sender_full_name": "Sebastian Ullrich",
        "timestamp": 1777805899
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ah, so the private variables still appear in the local context interactively, you just get an error upon using them?</p>",
        "id": 592599677,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Murrills",
        "timestamp": 1777847302
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><em>Some</em> context let's say, to be figured out!</p>",
        "id": 592675613,
        "sender_full_name": "Sebastian Ullrich",
        "timestamp": 1777883150
    }
]